        "title": "Temple of Shiva",
        "text": "This is usually the first place shown to you on your visit to Kathmandu during sight seeing.\nLeather articles and photos are not allowed inside the temple premises although you can take snaps outside the temple.\nThe diety here has four faces , in case you need to perfrom pooja a token is to be taken one day prior to your visit. When we entered temple we could see line at 4 different doors , not sure which one to take we managed to take all 4 spending some time in the line.The shivling is huge so you dont have to struggle looking at it. \nFor photos when you come out of the temple wear your shoes and walk across the creamtion area to the small hill opposite the temple. Perhaps you can have good snaps of the locality and the  temple. You have benches there to spend time. You can also come across sadhus engaged in photo shoot for a fee.",
